RESOURCE ENVELOPE
Per-step routed activation/resource packets:

35.

This fixed packet count is the focused H61 hard-envelope proxy.

No policy may route more than:
35 units per step.

TARGET-FREE CURRENT DEMAND
Each active emitter contributes:

stake
*
current emitter trust

into its local demand source.

The demand signal diffuses locally.

Packets see only:
neighbor field values.

No target coordinates
or
global distance.

TOPOLOGY DAMAGE
A central-right tissue block becomes unavailable during:
steps 420..499.

Routing must use remaining local topology.

No resource is created by the damage.

COMPARATORS

NO-MORPHOLOGY
Uses:
dual-timescale emitter trust
+
sparse re-audit
+
target-free diffusive field.

Transport conductance remains:
1.

NAIVE COUPLED FEEDBACK
Uses:
fast/slow emitter trust

and
reinforces every delivered traffic path
whether delivery succeeds or not.

Conductance decays very slowly.

Thus:

MORE TRAFFIC
->
MORE CONDUCTANCE
->
MORE FUTURE TRAFFIC.

BOUNDED DEVELOPMENTAL METABOLISM
Uses:
fast emitter expression trust
+
slow retained credibility
+
sparse re-audit
+
rare-critical trust floor
+
target-free demand field
+
DIRECTED transport memory
+
reinforcement ONLY after successful functional uptake
+
substantial conductance decay.

This is the integrated H56-H60 working architecture.

