PRIMARY NAIVE-COUPLING NEGATIVE
Naive trust/flow/morphology coupling creates:

POSITIVE-FEEDBACK LOCK-IN.

The chronic false sink receives:
more traffic
than in the no-morphology baseline.

The temporarily failed sink continues to receive almost all possible service.

Transport conductance:
nearly doubles on average
and
saturates individual edges.

Thus:

REPEATED TRAFFIC
CAN BECOME
SELF-JUSTIFYING TRANSPORT AUTHORITY.

The integrated failure is primarily:
hysteretic lock-in
rather than:
a clean oscillatory instability
at this working point.

